CHANGED: The cleanup phase that flattens the function hierarchy got substantially faster: inlining a function no longer rebuilds the unchanged parts of the caller, and the evaluator-backed transformations run once per flattening iteration instead of in every settle round of its inner fixpoint. On large designs this removes about a third of total compile time. As a side effect the generated HDL can differ slightly: an alias for a field selection may now be inlined into its use sites.
